# 🏙️ Smart City Service Portal — Project Summary

## Overview

A **full-stack Java web application** built as a **B.Tech 2nd Year Java PBL (Project-Based Learning)** submission. It simulates a real-world municipal service platform where citizens can interact with city services digitally, and admins can manage everything from a central dashboard.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| **Language** | Java 11 |
| **Web Framework** | Java Servlet + JSP (MVC) |
| **View Layer** | JSP + JSTL 1.2 |
| **Database** | MySQL 8.0+ |
| **DB Access** | JDBC (PreparedStatement) |
| **Build Tool** | Maven 3.6+ |
| **Server** | Apache Tomcat 9/10 |
| **Styling** | Vanilla CSS (Dark Mode UI) |
| **Session Mgmt** | HttpSession |
| **Security** | Role-Based Access Control (ADMIN / CITIZEN) |

---

## 🏗️ Architecture — MVC Pattern

```
Browser Request
     ↓
  Servlet (Controller)        ← Handles HTTP logic, routing, session checks
     ↓
  DAO (Model/DB Layer)        ← Executes SQL via JDBC, returns Java objects
     ↓  ↑
  MySQL Database              ← smartcity_db with 5 tables
     ↓
  JSP (View)                  ← Renders HTML using JSTL / EL
     ↓
Browser Response
```

